  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I started out excitedly, with hopes in my heart, expecting a beginning like Oasis in Ready Player One or Oz in Summer Wars, but I was immediately disappointed when I started. I had imagined a traditional MMORPG with a vibrant lobby where I could be anything I wanted to be and do anything I wanted to do, and a bunch of great worlds to explore. I didn't know what to do in my first world. I was also expecting the most popular VR content, but it started with no one there and was silent. Every time the only sound was the lonely echo of the controls, I felt my mind drift away from VRchat.\n\nI'm not saying to have a grand opening, I'm just saying that if I could have stepped out into a vibrant public lobby with the same country users by reading the IP, the outcome might have been different. The Japanese cluster metaverse has been around for a long time now, and the first thing you do over there is meet other users in the lobby, please implement a lobby in VRchat as well. Even if that is a privilege of VRC+.\n\nI hope those of you who can agree with me will keep your requests up on VRChat's Canary (where you can give feedback). I'm not sure if I'll ever get around to trying VRChat again someday, but maybe the lobby server will be ready.",
